To whom it may concern,

I'm writing to report an active animal welfare hazard at a construction site located at 9505 Sheldon Road, Elk Grove, CA 95624. A dog has been confined to a crate at this site for an extended period. While someone appears to be providing food and water, the dog is being kept in these conditions during extreme heat, which poses an immediate risk to its health and life.

I understand that an animal services or law enforcement visit has already occurred, but the dog remains on-site under these conditions. Given the urgency of heat exposure, I'm asking that this be treated as an immediate hazard requiring prompt inspection and removal for a vet check-up.

I'm requesting:

1: Immediate inspection of the site;
2: Coordination with Elk Grove Animal Services regarding the dog's condition and removal if warranted;
3: Enforcement action against the property/site owner if violations of the Municipal Code are confirmed;
4: A status update on the action taken.

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-UXFq_TPU4N_eW_uhvEjQMdIQNw1UM8z/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
contact@hallieforanimals.org

To whom it may concern,

A dog reported at or near 3280 R St, Merced, CA 95348 is being kept muzzled continuously through the current 100°F+ heat. A muzzle worn for prolonged periods prevents a dog from panting, the primary way dogs shed heat, placing her at serious risk of heat injury or death in these temperatures.

We are requesting that Merced County Sheriff's Animal Services:

1: Conduct an immediate welfare check at this location;
2: Assess whether continuous muzzling in current temperatures is impairing the dog's ability to pant and thermoregulate;
3: Take protective custody of the dog under California Penal Code § 597.1 if her condition warrants;
4: Ensure she receives a veterinary evaluation.

California Penal Code § 597.1 authorizes officers to seize an animal, without a prior warrant, where they have reasonable grounds to believe prompt action is required to protect its health or safety. We ask that you act on that authority.

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1my7RTrKbdgG6DZFBPalcF9Q1Kv10b6IM/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
contact@hallieforanimals.org

To whom it may concern,

Two long-haired German Shepherds are reported to be confined 24/7 to a small outdoor kennel on Nokota Way, Roseville, CA 95747. Neighbors report these concerns have been raised with Animal Control since 2024, and that the dogs have been kept in this kennel continuously for at least two years.

Following Animal Control contact with the owners, the enclosure was reportedly covered further with tarps and wooden panels. In current 100°F+ temperatures, reduced airflow inside a covered kennel places the dogs at serious risk of heat injury.

Referencing Case # 2026-47341, we are requesting that you:

1: Conduct an immediate welfare check at this location;
2: Assess whether the enclosure provides adequate ventilation, shade, shelter, and water given the added coverings and current temperatures;
3: Review the prior reports on this address dating back to 2024;
4: Take protective custody of both dogs under California Penal Code § 597.1 if their condition warrants;
5: Ensure both dogs receive a veterinary evaluation;

California Penal Code § 597.1 authorizes officers to seize an animal, without a prior warrant, where they have reasonable grounds to believe prompt action is required to protect its health or safety. We ask that you act on that authority.

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tbNVogW6GXKb25NeeN4r5sQjlTNS9WtO/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
contact@hallieforanimals.org

İlgili makamlara,

Tuzla’da, belediye ekipleri 18 yaşındaki bir köpeği yakalamak üzere bir konut kompleksine girdiklerinde, olay yerine gelen polis memurları yakın mesafeden bir kadın gönüllünün gözlerine doğrudan biber gazı sıktı. Kadın, ambulansla hastaneye kaldırıldı. Gönüllüler ayrıca kollarından tutularak itildi.

Bu güç kullanımının orantılılığı ve yasallığı konusunda hesap sorulmasını talep ediyor ve yetkililerden şunları istiyoruz:

1: Olayla ilgili memur(lar)ın kimliklerinin tespit edilmesini ve idari ve cezai soruşturmaların açılmasını;
2: Gözlere yakın mesafeden biber gazı sıkılmasının, polisin güç kullanımıyla ilgili yasa (PVSK Ek Madde 6) ve orantılılık ilkesine uygun olup olmadığını değerlendirsin ve gerekirse Türk Ceza Kanunu’nun 256. maddesi (güç kullanma yetkisini aşma) uyarınca işlem yapsın;
3: Olayla ilgili tüm görüntüleri (polis kameraları, güvenlik kameraları, görgü tanıklarının kayıtları) muhafaza etsin ve incelesin;

Video kanıtı: https://drive.google.com/file/d/14YlA_itCiQv2iN-38iF8-9rXRw4rliAs/view?usp=sharing

Saygılarımızla,



@HallieForAnimals Ekibi
contact@hallieforanimals.org




To whom it may concern,

In Tuzla, as municipal teams entered a residential complex to seize an 18-year-old dog, the responding police officer(s) deployed pepper spray at close range directly into the eyes of a woman volunteer. She was taken to hospital by ambulance. Volunteers were also grabbed by the arms and shoved.

We request accountability for the proportionality and lawfulness of this force, and ask that the authorities:

1: Identify the officer(s) involved and open administrative and criminal investigations;
2: Assess whether close-range pepper spray to the eyes complied with the law on police use of force (PVSK Add. Art. 6) and the principle of proportionality, and pursue action under Turkish Penal Code Art. 256 (exceeding the authority to use force) if warranted;
3: Preserve and review all footage of the incident (police cameras, CCTV, bystander recordings);

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/14YlA_itCiQv2iN-38iF8-9rXRw4rliAs/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
contact@hallieforanimals.org

To whom it may concern,

I'm writing to demand an investigation into the death of a dog, Rocko, in DeSoto, and the conditions that led to it.

A neighbor witnessed Rocko kept outside for extended periods in extreme Texas heat, repeatedly warned the owners to bring him inside, and the dog died. The owners are Frankie and Barbara Washington, who own and operate Paradise Funeral Home (3910 S. Lancaster Rd, Dallas).

Under Texas Penal Code § 42.092, failing to provide an animal necessary care or shelter, and causing an animal's death through cruel neglect, is a criminal offense. This account describes that conduct and warrants a full investigation.

I am asking that you:

1: Open a cruelty investigation under Texas Penal Code § 42.092;
2: Take the witnessing neighbor's first-hand account;
3: Establish the cause and circumstances of Rocko's death, including any veterinary or necropsy evidence;
4: Assess the welfare of any other animals in the household;

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/13DAp06M0CgXfm7qxeQCBEyIG3iU2bFRH/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
contact@hallieforanimals.org

To whom it may concern,

I am writing to report a suspected dogfighting operation in Simpson County and to request an immediate investigation and welfare seizure.

Bryson Mills, the sole proprietor of B & B Mills Transportation LLC, which lists 133 Donnie Norwood Rd, Mendenhall, MS 39114, has been posted to social media showing himself with pit bulls kept on heavy chains, and a pit bull with most of its face missing. Chained yard dogs and catastrophic facial injuries of this kind are recognized indicators of organized dogfighting, and each is independently a serious crime under Mississippi law.

Under Miss. Code Ann. § 97-41-19, it is a felony to sponsor, stage, or conduct a dogfight, to own a dog with intent to fight it, or to train or transport a dog for a fight. The mutilation of a dog is felony aggravated cruelty under Miss. Code Ann. § 97-41-16. A court may order seizure of these animals on probable cause established by a witness's sworn account (§ 97-41-2), and an officer making an arrest may seize the dogs and all fighting paraphernalia (§ 97-41-19(3)).

Because this individual operates a transportation business and fighting rings routinely move dogs across state lines, this also falls within federal jurisdiction under the Animal Welfare Act's animal-fighting prohibition (7 U.S.C. § 2156). I ask that your office coordinate with the FBI Jackson Field Office and the USDA Office of Inspector General accordingly.

I demand that the Simpson County Sheriff's Office:

1: Conduct a welfare check and, on probable cause, seize every dog at 133 Donnie Norwood Rd under § 97-41-2 and § 97-41-19(3), with immediate veterinary examination;
2: Open a criminal investigation of Bryson Mills for dogfighting and aggravated cruelty under § 97-41-19 and § 97-41-16, including the training and transport provisions;
3: Preserve the social media posts and all related evidence and pursue seizure of any fighting paraphernalia (chains, treadmills, breaking sticks, veterinary supplies);
4: Coordinate with the FBI Jackson Field Office and USDA-OIG on the interstate-commerce and transport dimensions under 7 U.S.C. § 2156;
5: Issue a public statement confirming the investigation and release its findings once concluded.

These animals cannot wait. Please act now.

Video evidence: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TRaIc2Onq81b8HNx_zuzvRcX47PKwUrC/view?usp=sharing

Sincerely,



@HallieForAnimals Team
